    {
      "id": "1557373128546590850",
      "type": "Reply",
      "timestamp": "2026-10-07T12:44:48.439+00:00",
      "timestampEdited": null,
      "callEndedTimestamp": null,
      "isPinned": false,
      "content": "When I was meeting with Poh I asked first, \"do you know anyone at Kulicke & Soffa\" as they are headquartered near my hotel and they make the (best, most, one of those words) wirebonders and he said no. \nI then asked  \"do you know *any* wirebonders?\" \nAnd he said \"Yeah! Literally downstairs, you want me to call him?\"\nI obviously said yes lol. \nThe guy didn't really have a lot of useful information that was sharable. He sent me to this [product](https://www.yamaha-robotics.com/en/products/process/utc-rz1) and while it does have specs it wasn't what I was hoping for. \n\nThe one dimension I kept asking about was the length based on die height. The spec we used said 1.5x height, @stuart said 2x, but this guy was very adamant those were wrong and you can go super close, it depends on the capillary you get. He drew some stuff on the whiteboard for me and then erased it before I could take a pic. He then pointed me at this company [SPT](https://www.smallprecisiontools.com/shortcuts-en/publications-downloads/semiconductor-bonding-tools-downloads/?oid=120&lang=en) There's a bunch of stuff to read there, but haven't clicked a link, but they sell the capillaries.",
